{
  "dom_id": "step-q100054",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Simplify the expression $\\frac{6x}{5}+15-\\frac{4x}{7}+8.$",
  "worked_solution": "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x}{5}+15-\\frac{4x}{7}+8 & = \\\\ (\\frac{6x}{5}-\\frac{4x}{7})+(15+8) & = \\\\ (\\frac{42x}{35}-\\frac{20x}{35})+(15+8) & = \\\\ (\\frac{42x-20x}{35})+23 & = \\\\ \\frac{22x}{35}+23\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
